WEBVTT

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.910
Hey, Amara...

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.040
Have you ever thought that the wind felt good?

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:22.870
The wind?

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.710
What are you talking about?

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.460
Having your morning coffee?

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.920
CEO Kube...

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.970
Good morning!

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:34.090
It's fine. Please sit.

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:36.970
Research and Development Division 3 has informed me

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:41.770
that the Machine Goodfellow trials are underway.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.390
So I thought I'd pay you a visit.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.020
To be honest, we're more than happy to assist Macbeth Enterprises in this.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:52.400
There's no doubt we'll meet your expectations,

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:54.320
and we will of course repay you for your assistance.

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:57.030
Amara, Moco...

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.080
You two are very important to me.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:04.160
My special test pilots...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:09.130
But remember that when I say "special," I'm not only referring to your abilities.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.380
Do not forget that.

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.880
I consider myself to be more than just your boss—

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.970
I consider myself to be your father.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:30.770
All the laughter, all the tears—everything happened just to meet you

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:31.440
Always go

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:34.860
On my own

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.070
Always go

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:49.710
The wind blows my overflowing tears away (the wind blows them away)

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:57.090
I try to reach out my hand time after time toward what's to come

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:03.180
I've been hurt before by careless words

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:12.110
It's time I move forward with that unchangeable past

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.650
All the laughter, all the tears—

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:25.290
everything that has happened brought me to you

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:31.330
All we have left is the future

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:37.760
Please become our reason to continue living

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:44.470
And then the sun will once again shine on us

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.150
If you ever need anything,

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.610
don't be afraid to come to me.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:57.650
Let's have dinner sometime soon.

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.320
Thank you, sir.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:08.910
Aren't they good kids?

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.870
I'm so glad that another research team

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:16.840
kept them overseas during the Kanda incident.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.260
I'm a good kid, too.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:24.970
Won't you invite me to dinner?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.270
Hey, you want to get dinner tonight?

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.980
Is that an order, Commander?

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.480
It might be about half work-related, I suppose.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.730
Please don't mix work with your personal life.

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:43.990
I feel like all the color is draining out of my world.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:48.870
That's Governor Yomatsuri, from aboard the <i>Tenkaido</i>.

00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:51.710
Good morning.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:53.000
Morning.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:57.500
Arashi Eiji is still thought to be missing, is he not?

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.510
Unfortunately, yes.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.720
This is a problem...

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:06.800
HQ won't overlook any actions that could interfere with the Kivotos Plan.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:10.680
You tried to kidnap him, didn't you?

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.100
Your eyes gave you away.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.810
Seeing that pitiful look on your face is enough for me this time, though.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.110
I won't report this, but you owe me.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.150
Commander, this conversation is being hacked.

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:23.910
Impossible!

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.240
Pfft. You found me?

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.080
Akari!

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:31.870
Akari!

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.500
Morning, Mom...

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.960
Dad tried to hit on Rita again this morning, and got rejected.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.420
You have this room bugged, as well?

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:44.220
Nope, I just took a random guess.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:50.260
You're part of Globe now. You work for me.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:54.890
Must we go over what is and is not acceptable again?

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.020
How did you even get into the secure line, anyway?

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.190
Magic! It's magic!

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.280
That's forbidden! Magic is now forbidden!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.950
Hey, what do you guys really think about the Kivotos Plan?

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:17.290
It's a colonial operation meant to allow humanity to escape Earth, should the worst happen.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.290
Humanity's elected representatives

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.170
all voted unanimously in favor of the plan.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:27.760
What you mean is that the Globe Federation voted unanimously, not humanity.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:33.020
At the very least, I'm not interested in survival through a plan like that.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.140
The Kivotos Plan is still classified top-secret...

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:41.190
If you learn anything else about it, I'll have no choice but to arrest you.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.030
And in the end, I'm just in the way.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:47.660
Logical, logical... It's time for Akari to disappear!

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.160
Kivotos Plan

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.830
I'm a bad mother...

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.380
This is Alpha Sector's surveillance footage.

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.350
Since the last battle, that Kill-T-Gang Type-3 has taken no action

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:13.970
beyond floating through this area.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:19.690
Impactor Weinstock is currently deployed to that area.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:20.860
Maintain surveillance.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:23.820
Are we really not going to attack it?

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.530
For the moment, we're merely observing.

00:06:25.990 --> 00:06:28.860
That is Globe HQ's decision.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.870
Yes, it's Globe HQ's decision.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.620
And his wish, as well.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.790
But the commander hasn't actually granted permission, has he?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.340
I'm impressed.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.340
He, of course, is not nearly as good as Teppei,

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.590
but he's already mastered the basic controls.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.350
I've always been good at games like this.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.220
You can't treat this like a game.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:01.480
I think that he understands that better than we do.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:05.690
You're not used to sustained training like this, so that's enough for today.

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.530
I'm still fine.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:09.610
Well, she was worried enough to come to see you.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.960
After the Kivotos Plan members evacuate,

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:32.470
the Kill-T-Gang will end all remaining human life on Earth.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:39.270
The Kill-T-Gang will then navigate itself out of the solar system.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.140
Isn't that right?

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:44.060
They behave like some sort of space vampire.

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.860
If their existence requires Orgone energy on a planetary scale,

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:53.240
they're unlikely to remain here after nearly all of humanity has died.

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:56.620
You are our planet's most advanced artificial intelligence.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.740
I am, indeed.

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:00.540
Pac does not lie.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.500
This unprecedented threat toward Earth

00:08:05.500 --> 00:08:11.630
will in fact turn this planet into a utopia for those people whom I've chosen.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:16.010
Fate has decreed that I be the arbiter of human life...

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.440
Hey, Tsutomu...

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:34.700
Hope is believing that the future will be better than today.

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:39.330
And real hope can only be created with our own choices!

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.720
Toshiaki...

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:03.100
Where is Daichi?

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.030
Is your head feeling better?

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.610
Yeah, I'm fine now.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.200
Hana...

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:22.200
Do you remember the first time we met?

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:22.830
Yup.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.370
And what you said then?

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:27.540
Yup.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:37.470
A dream, an echo singing of pleasant memories

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:47.520
It glows like that promise I'm sure we made

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.530
Is that you?

00:09:56.990 --> 00:10:06.460
It reaches the lonely depths of my soul

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:00.950
What did that mean?

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:06.500
I've been on this island for a long time, but I'm not originally from here.

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:15.800
It's reminding me of a wait somewhere someday

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:11.130
I was created to fire the Livlaster.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:15.010
But I couldn't do it.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:25.270
The future blooms in front of my eyes

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.880
A long time ago...

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:24.010
My world was veiled entirely in darkness.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:29.100
So I set off to seek you

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:35.480
To say our goodbyes

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:31.610
Shadows surrounded me on all sides,

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:36.280
and the only thing they wanted me to do was fire that gun.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:44.790
A dream, a love blooming like the sun in the sky

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:42.910
I wasn't even sure that I wanted to give them what they wanted, though...

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:47.790
But then, I thought I saw a light.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:54.500
It's the light of a day when it was my turn to do the protecting

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:54.170
It felt like someone's voice calling out to me.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.470
I knew that I needed to meet that person...

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.300
That I <i>wanted</i> to meet that person.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:13.770
It's telling me that I lost nothing

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:23.160
Because the smile on your face never fades

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:23.450
So I broke free of the darkness and ran toward the light.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:31.790
Please, my dear future, don't cry

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.250
And this is the place I ran to.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:36.050
By "them," do you mean those Planetary Gear guys?

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:42.930
Our paths may meet again someday

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:40.670
As Planetary Gears, our real bodies are constructed

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:43.430
of a material called Ego Blocks.

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:52.560
A dream, an echo singing of pleasant memories

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:47.770
They are crystallized, digitized souls.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:53.310
Unless even our Ego Blocks are destroyed, we are theoretically immortal.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:12:01.530
It glows like that promise I'm sure we made

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:58.230
We believe that we are the galaxy's only true inhabitants.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:04.030
Everything and everyone else are nothing but tools for our uses.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:06.330
It gently strokes my cheek

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.740
I don't have an Ego Block body.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:11.120
Like sunlight through the trees

00:12:08.700 --> 00:12:10.580
I'm not actually one of them.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:14.960
I was meant to be nothing more than a tool used to fire the Livlaster.

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:21.260
And I tie it all into a bouquet meant for you

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.420
You're not a tool... You're a person.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:22.010
They don't think so.

00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:27.510
But Teppei's different.

00:12:29.260 --> 00:12:32.810
Teppei, do you still have your personality and memories

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:35.850
from when you were Albion?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.400
What does the world look like to you?

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:50.910
We Planetary Gears might be like the glass bead

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:53.370
in this Ramune bottle.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.380
Even when you've drunk it all and the bottle's job is done,

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.340
the bead is still stuck inside.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.460
Eternal life...

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.050
Does that in turn mean eternal happiness?

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:08.760
Or does it just mean eternal spiritual imprisonment?

00:13:10.310 --> 00:13:11.970
I'm hungry.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:13.390
Let's eat lunch.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.350
I'll make something awesome!

00:13:17.310 --> 00:13:19.230
What should I cook?

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:28.240
You spend a lot of time alone in the computer room.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.580
Indeed, I treasure the occasional moment of quiet thought.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.790
It is my very own sanctuary...

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:43.510
The lock to that room opens only when presented with my own biometric data.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:47.130
I am the only one who can talk to Pac.

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:50.260
This weak security isn't even a challenge.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:58.940
How have you been, Pac?

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:02.820
Welcome back, Lady Malkin and Lord Amarok!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:07.950
Kube Masaki hasn't actually figured out who we are yet, has he?

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:10.820
He's a very self-centered man, you see.

00:14:10.820 --> 00:14:14.160
That narrows his outlook considerably, and makes him rather easy to deal with.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:17.040
So you have no complaints about life here?

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:24.250
Being a useful tool to the Planetary Gears is my sole pleasure in life.

00:14:24.250 --> 00:14:25.960
Delightful...

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.260
Useful tools are always treated well.

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:33.260
I want you to prove your usefulness.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.350
I think you understand already,

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:41.060
but her presence is essential to the Kivotos Plan.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.480
Over.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.230
Understood.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:47.030
I'll deliver the flower to her vase.

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:08.220
Uncle?

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:11.890
Hana!

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:24.310
Mr. Nishikubo, I asked you to send Daichi home immediately.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.610
And you assured me that you would.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.190
Commander...

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.950
Please let me explain things to my uncle.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:31.160
Commander?

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:33.030
That's my job.

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:35.080
What does he mean by "Commander"?!

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:36.080
Mr. Toshiaki...

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.660
He's a minor!

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:40.000
What do you have him doing here without his guardian's knowledge?!

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.250
Please, Commander...

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:43.960
Leave me alone with my uncle for a while.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:47.090
All right.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:51.880
Even when your grades started to slip, I wasn't concerned.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.600
You've always been a good kid.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.180
So it's not like I'm against you getting out and doing something like traveling

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.890
on your own over summer vacation.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:04.400
If it's just for vacation, there's nothing to worry about.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:08.030
But it's different if you're planning to actually stay on Tanegashima...

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:12.860
It's not just the fact that Umi and my brother left you in my charge. You're precious to me.

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:15.990
More than anything else, you're my family!

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:22.160
What you're doing here puts you in danger, doesn't it?

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:25.880
Uncle...

00:16:26.880 --> 00:16:29.050
I'm truly grateful for what you've done.

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.760
You've always looked out for me.

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:34.970
But I...

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:41.930
My world was veiled entirely in darkness.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:47.860
I felt trapped living in that city, too.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:53.200
I never actually felt that I belonged there.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:14.880
Pitz?

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:17.510
Dangerous? What is?

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:21.600
You seem to be enjoying your freedom.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:27.940
This is the kind of thing that happens when you go outside on your own.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:33.240
I know you're not sure what you want to do with your life.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:36.860
What's wrong, Pitz?

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:38.740
Ow!

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:40.410
What'd you do that for?

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.920
Did something happen to Hana?

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:50.880
Hana!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:52.590
Daichi!

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.840
Ah, so the Earth Driver has arrived?

00:17:56.680 --> 00:17:57.220
Daichi!

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:01.510
D-Daichi!

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:02.720
Uncle!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:04.390
Get back!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.100
But...

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:06.810
Get back!

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.400
I'm sorry, Uncle.

00:18:11.060 --> 00:18:12.820
This is my problem.

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:15.860
Don't take another step.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.200
What are you doing?

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.700
I'm taking Mutou Hana.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.620
This is the right choice.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:30.380
What is he...

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.590
Release Hana!

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:38.590
Are you prepared to shoot me?

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.140
I'm asking if you're prepared to kill someone!

00:18:45.770 --> 00:18:47.140
That's right...

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:49.190
You aren't ready to do that.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:52.400
You can't save anyone like that.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:55.820
You're nothing more than an insignificant brat with a Livlaster!

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:00.910
What are you doing, kid?!

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:01.570
Hana!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:08.960
Hana!

00:19:10.870 --> 00:19:11.670
Are you okay?

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:18.340
At that moment, I wondered if maybe the voice

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:21.930
that had led Hana to this planet was my own...

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:23.760
No.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:26.060
I wanted it to be me.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.060
Daichi, are you okay?

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.480
I'm okay...

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:36.650
Are you all right, Mr. Toshiaki?

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:38.990
Mr. Nishikubo...

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:44.070
Am I correct to suspect that something just happened...

00:19:44.070 --> 00:19:45.580
No, that something <i>will</i> happen...

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:49.290
That normal people like me can't understand?

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:52.620
I cannot answer that.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.420
You don't need to worry.

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.420
I won't tell anyone what I saw here.

00:19:57.420 --> 00:19:58.510
Mr. Toshiaki...

00:19:59.340 --> 00:20:01.340
Just tell me one thing.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:06.470
Is Daichi trying to do something here that only he can do?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:08.810
Yes.

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:15.980
I felt a strength in his words that I've never seen from him before.

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:20.570
I always thought this day would come.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:27.780
He really is my brother's—Manatsu Taiyo's—son.

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:35.580
Hirosue Reito has been turned over to Salty Dog.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:40.010
The Ark Faction is becoming bolder.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:45.300
They will take any measure they deem necessary to ensure that the Kivotos Plan succeeds,

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:47.720
and that humanity's chosen survive.

00:20:47.720 --> 00:20:50.060
The only other way to deal with the Kill-T-Gangs is to

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.980
deploy the Impactors in accordance with the Interception Faction.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:56.860
Globe has supported both plans.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:59.730
Why do they have to oppose each other?

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:03.450
Since you're the deputy commander, I want to show you something.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.660
What's this?

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.200
Footage from the dark side of the Moon.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.040
Only a few people within Globe,

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:14.290
and nobody else in the world, have access to this feed.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:18.880
Eight years ago, the approach of the Kill-T-Gang Type-1 alone was enough to drain

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:22.210
the few dozen personnel stationed at Daedalus base

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.800
of their libidos, killing them instantly.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:28.180
The inexplicable burst phenomenon that occurred at that time

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:30.680
left the dark side of the Moon in this state.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:36.230
And this is how the Earth will look after a successful Kill-T-Gang attack.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:39.110
But even amongst the rest of Intercept Faction,

00:21:39.110 --> 00:21:41.860
who also believe we can stop them, aren't you considered an extremist?

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:43.320
That's right.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:47.860
The Kivotos Plan means the de facto extermination of humanity!

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:50.330
I refuse to accept it.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:54.620
You said that they're capable of stripping somebody's libido simply by being near them.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:59.000
But Daichi fought them at close range in the Earth Engine.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:00.210
How did he survive?

00:22:00.630 --> 00:22:04.460
We believe that is the Livlaster's doing.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:08.680
The gun's Orgone energy seems to protect him.

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:14.020
But even if Manatsu Daichi can fire the Livlaster,

00:22:14.020 --> 00:22:16.940
that doesn't change the fact that our situation is nearly hopeless.

00:22:16.940 --> 00:22:18.560
No...

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:24.320
Tell me, Taiyo...

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:28.820
You protected Earth and humanity...

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:31.950
How can I do the same?

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:54.970
The gentle breeze sweeps away even tears

00:22:54.970 --> 00:23:00.440
Even the recollections of the way of the stars

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:05.280
aren't always good things

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:12.950
I met you again on that faraway day

00:23:12.950 --> 00:23:22.420
Even though we're as close as we are, this distant day is beginning

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:30.630
You can hear my voice calling out when I'm all alone

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:36.640
More than just love, it's hard to put into words

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:42.520
I'm searching for what to say while I walk beside you

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:45.570
Instead of saying goodbye,

00:23:45.570 --> 00:23:53.740
I'll just put these love spun tears in my right pocket again tomorrow

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:57.160
Love is spreading across the world

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:03.290
And I finally found it, by your side

00:24:13.010 --> 00:24:16.640
Is humanity already doomed?

00:24:17.220 --> 00:24:23.520
Is getting a few chosen people out really our only hope?

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:27.770
And the Kill-T-Gang attacks Earth again.

00:24:28.650 --> 00:24:30.570
But during that battle...

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:34.030
Next time, on episode 7 of <i>Captain Earth</i>:

00:24:34.030 --> 00:24:37.200
The Midsummer's Knights.

00:24:34.030 --> 00:24:37.200
The Midsummer's Knights

00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:40.700
There's still a single hope.
